[Music]  this morning gulf coast residents  continued to deal with the aftermath of  hurricane laura which caused damage far  inland as well it arrived just before  the anniversary of a more destructive  storm  15 years ago this weekend hurricane  katrina  made landfall devastating new orleans  and the surrounding region  soon after one non-profit group got to  work  first in new orleans and now far and  wide helping homeowners pick up the  pieces  and rebuild their future  we just started a three-year 10 million  dollar campaign to rebuild 240 houses  hello young people  when we first met zach rosenberg and his  wife liz mccartney in 2015  their non-profit the saint bernard  project had rebuilt  614 homes in the new orleans area  it was kind of like the field of dreams  you build it and it would come  volunteers started coming out of the  wooden work one two  three today  sbp as it's now known has helped rebuild  more than 2500 homes  and the mission has expanded we just  built the first  net zero apartment building in all of  louisiana that means  solar panels powering batteries and 50  of those units are for veterans  rosenberg  says everything changed after meeting  world war  ii vet edward lee five years ago  we met the 94 year old who built his own  home  with his own hands home means  a hundred percent of my life katrina's  winds blew part of his roof off and  cracked his foundation  he patched up what he could with fema  money but ran  out before the job was done you never  thought of moving out of this house  no i'm gonna die  but not before volunteers made his house  whole again  he lived another three years and died  his family says  a happy man getting to know mr lee  changed the way we saw  our work it wasn't about building houses  and we're still doing more than ever  before  but it was about preventing the need to  rebuild the houses in the first place  since our last report sbp has gone  national  the nonprofit has helped homeowners from  missouri to the mid-atlantic  to the caribbean they've done it by  streamlining the  operation cutting in half the time it  takes to build a house  this houston home was refurbished with  roofing able to withstand  135 mile per hour winds and that  preparedness extends to cutting through  red tape the first way to do it is help  people understand and mitigate their  risk  we just got to 19 million people by july  to educate them on flood insurance and  as important we train people after  disaster to navigate the system  to avoid contractor fraud to navigate  fema  to work with insurance so it sounds to  me like you front load  resources to them before they even need  them absolutely  the mission has become a calling for  rosenberg and mccartney  who picked up and moved to new orleans  15 years ago  how's everybody a spirit of sacrifice  needed now  more than ever here we are two  hurricanes in the gulf  you have fires in the west you have  tornadoes and other storms throughout  the midwest  how do you ratchet up when it's coming  at you from so many different sides  so we have deployment calls we are ready  to respond to  any disaster that hits within 36 hours  this year even with covid local  volunteers  who if and when something happens can  immediately  be there in their own community because  i'll tell you this michelle one of our  country's biggest assets  is the concern that fellow people have  for fellow citizens people from across  the country  who have gone to disaster to help other  people and they're ready to do it again  and i think frankly that will be very  healing at this time  and sbp has helped people in the region  impacted by hurricane laura and they say  they already have their teams in place  assessing the damage as we speak so  they're really gearing up  for today because today is when they're  actually getting on the ground  it's so many steps ahead then we then so  many were  back with katrina because of them and  this is just one non-profit there are  many others  so they can pop up so quickly now i mean  and just take action and and it's not  just  built rebuilding the home to prevent it  from being damaged in the next one it is  those relationships right  between the workers yes it's really a  joy to see  mr lee stayed in touch with all the  folks who worked in his home it was  quite level yeah great yeah

